.TH EPOLL_PWAIT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
epoll_pwait \- Linux x86-64 syscall 281
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B int epoll_pwait(int epoll, void* events, int maximum, int timeout, const sigset_t* mask);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waits for epoll events with an optional eight-byte kernel signal mask. Events use the packed 12-byte Linux x86-64 layout.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR epoll_pwait (2)
